def document(reports):
    lines=['# Americas: exhaustive geographic semantic follow-up','','Reviewed 2 October 2026. Both current American continental chains are inventoried from continent down to every location. This is a complete inventory and country-specific source-policy assessment, **not completed semantic approval**. Original land/urban/island evidence and individual exceptions remain explicit open gates. No geography, historical content or prepared display asset changes in these reports.','','The durable ledgers are [`north-america.json.gz`](../../data/geographic-semantic-followup/north-america.json.gz) and [`south-america.json.gz`](../../data/geographic-semantic-followup/south-america.json.gz). Every current ID has complete direct membership, exact footprint/member hash, source role/vintage/license, inherited checks, new source evidence and applicable proposal. Deterministic gzip prevents individual tracked files exceeding the Site source-file limit; these complete research ledgers are not added to static website assets.','','## Coverage by tier','','| Continent | Locations | Provinces | Areas | Regions | Subcontinents | Reference-owner contexts |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
    for d in reports:
        c=d['counts']; l=d['level_counts'];lines.append(f"| {d['continent']} | {c['locations']:,} | {l['province']} | {l['area']} | {l['region']} | {l['subcontinent']} | {c['reference_owner_groups']} |")
    lines+=['','Scope is determined by each location’s **actual full parent chain**, never the single continent label on a global owner group. Thus all mainland USA and French Guiana are included even though their shared owner profiles also occur elsewhere. Colombia, Venezuela and France span both ledgers. Antarctica is excluded. EU5 counts are no quotas.','','## Every regional branch','','| Continent / Region | Locations | Areas | Provinces | Assessment |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |']
    for d in reports:
        for r in sorted((g for g in d['groups'] if g['level']=='region'),key=lambda g:g['name']):
            loc=set(r['member_location_ids']); inside=collections.Counter(g['level'] for g in d['groups'] if set(g['member_location_ids'])<=loc)
            lines.append(f"| {d['continent']} / {r['name']} | {r['members']} | {inside['area']} | {inside['province']} | Open; every direct child and local source purpose recorded |")
    lines+=['','Mexico and Brazil-shaped region footprints still require country-independent physical or functional macro-geography. Census divisions and botanical reporting conventions supply specific source purposes; neither political borders nor an ADM integer establish an atlas tier. Central-American country-labelled botanical residuals crossing administrative parents also remain open.','','## Every represented country and territory','','The same review rubric applies everywhere: source role, vintage/license, local and urban purpose, neighboring units, anonymous remnants, multipart/island coverage and exact parent correspondence. Failed retrievals and landing pages without usable taxonomy are not counted as approval. All 39 applicable/global ADM policy metadata profiles were freshly retrieved; France and Netherlands European policies are explicitly distinguished from American fallback territories.','','| Continent | Profile / reference owner | Locations | Source-policy assessment |','| --- | --- | ---: | --- |']
    for d in reports:
        for c in sorted(d['countries'],key=lambda c:c['iso']):lines.append(f"| {d['continent']} | {c['iso']} — {c['reference_owner']} | {c['count']} | {c['assessment'].replace('|','/')} |")
    lines+=['','## New concrete blockers and source-supported proposals','','- **Ten live El Salvador `Null` labels**, not zero. Every original shape attribute, source/current geometry hash, bounds, geodesic area, retained-source share, land-mask diagnostic and independent district coverage is embedded. They include land and mixed coastal/border territory; no nearest-name rename or water-only deletion is justified. The previous zero-anonymous summary does not describe current geography.','- **Guatemala has two lake polygons treated as municipalities.** AMSA identifies Amatitlán and AMSCLAE identifies Atitlán; both exact IDs and source attributes are recorded. Natural Earth’s coarse land mask contains their interiors while its lake collection omits both. Correct water-body versus municipal semantics; obtaining complete inland-water proof and an explicit land-location policy precedes retirement or reassignment.','- **El Salvador HDX source counts include water.** Its actual 2024-valid geometry contains 266 district features and 48 municipal features, including four explicitly named lake/reservoir records. Those mean 262 districts + four waters and 44 municipalities + four waters; the provider counts are not legal subdivision totals. The original names, PCodes, areas and geometry hashes are preserved.','- **Trinidad omits Arima.** The original source has 14 features including Tobago; both its same-vintage CLGF profile and the ministry taxonomy identify 14 corporations on Trinidad plus distinct Tobago administration. Exact licensed source boundaries are still required before installation.','- **Guyana’s 27 features are not verified NDCs.** HDX says their role is currently unknown and unreconciled with population boundaries; CLGF documents 65 NDCs in 2017–18. The source-role description can be corrected without inventing local jurisdiction footprints.','- **Suriname source inventory contradicts its metadata.** Fresh pinned geometry contains 58 features, the API claims 62, and active geography has 59 adaptations. Reconcile exact source IDs, codes, legal vintage and source-parent geometry before filling guessed “missing” units.','- Every same-name provincial family is listed with all current IDs, exact children and footprint hashes. West Virginia/Hancock, Alaska/Aleutians West, Buenos Aires/Quilmes, Tierra del Fuego, Guatemala/Sololá, Central-American border portions, Wanica, Norte de Santander, Táchira and Valparaíso are distinguished from the 32 Canadian ecological families crossing different area parents. A shared label alone authorizes no merge.','- Exact archived-member candidates are recorded for Antigua/Barbuda/Redonda, Grenada/Southern Grenadines, Saint Kitts/Nevis, Saint Vincent/Grenadines, Saint-Pierre/Miquelon-Langlade and the three US Virgin Islands. Named-island source support does not waive full land coverage, licensed footprints, urban/local purpose or archived-history migration.','- Province-sized Peru/Bolivia/Uruguay/Belize locations, Brazil’s functional/rural aggregation and Canadian ecological replacements remain independently reviewable decisions. Candidate finer layers and their counts are not an approved replacement geography.','','## Current footprint diagnostics for all placeholder/water cases','','WGS84 geodesic areas are diagnostic, not equal-area quotas. The coastal land percentage uses Natural Earth 1:10m; it does not measure all inland water and cannot prove that a location is land-only or water-only.','','| ID | Current label | Original km² | Current km² | Coarse land % | Result |','| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |']
    for r in reports[0]['source_evidence']['diagnostics']['cases']:
        lines.append(f"| {r['id']} | {r['name']} | {r['original_wgs84_area_km2']:.3f} | {r['current_wgs84_area_km2']:.3f} | {100*r['diagnostic_land_mask']['land_mask_share']:.2f} | Identity/complete land-water classification open |")
    lines+=['','## Reproduce and resume','','```sh','python scripts/audit-americas-semantic-followup.py --check','python scripts/audit-americas-semantic-followup.py','```','','The committed compressed reports contain source receipts with exact URLs, byte hashes, parsed metadata, inspected facts, prepared-source named inventories, concrete source diagnostic properties and archived candidate memberships. Rebuilding or checking needs no previous-thread cache. New network observations must supply a new `--observations` file rather than relabeling old response bytes as newly fetched. The checks verify every current ID, complete chain, exact hashes, inherited closure inventory and documentation; they do not claim independent semantic approval.','','Geometry or membership migration must preserve stable IDs/archives and immutable historical claims, use an explicit source-backed crosswalk, regenerate derived ownership when footprints change, and rerun source-land/overlap/fixed-grid coverage gates. Every unresolved child branch remains open until independently supported; a structurally complete continent or source count cannot close it.','']
    return '\n'.join(lines)

def main():
    p=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--observations',type=pathlib.Path);p.add_argument('--check',action='store_true');args=p.parse_args()
    observations=read(args.observations) if args.observations else read(ROOT/'data/geographic-semantic-followup/north-america.json.gz')['source_evidence']
    reports=[build(slug,observations) for slug in CONTINENTS]
    for slug,result in zip(CONTINENTS,reports):
        path=ROOT/f'data/geographic-semantic-followup/{slug}.json.gz'
        if args.check: assert read(path)==result,f'{slug} report stale'
        else: path.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);path.write_bytes(gzip.compress(json.dumps(result,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':')).encode(),mtime=0))
        print(json.dumps({'continent':result['continent'],'counts':result['counts'],'levels':result['level_counts'],'report_bytes':path.stat().st_size,'report_sha256':digest(path)}))
    if args.check: assert DOC.read_text()==document(reports),'Americas documentation stale'
    else: DOC.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);DOC.write_text(document(reports))

if __name__=='__main__': main()
